#
# Build context for every image is the repo root (compose: `context: ..`).
#
# Without this file, docker/Dockerfile.web's `COPY web/ .` copied the host's
# web/node_modules over the fresh `npm ci` output from the deps stage. A stale
# web/node_modules on the VPS (manual install, 2026-04-18) meant every prod web
# image shipped April dependencies regardless of package-lock.json, so
# Dependabot alerts closed on the lockfile but the fixes never reached prod.
# Dependencies must only ever come from the lockfile inside the image.
**/node_modules
web/.next

# Context size only: no Dockerfile COPYs these (builds copy web/, src/ and
# docker/requirements*.txt). Locally they made the context ~1.9GB.
.git
.venv*
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
**/__pycache__
*.log
docs/Presentations
vscode-extension
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
web/coverage
